{
  "proposed_intent_examples": [],
  "composition_summary": "Preserved the single user message unchanged. Drafted one class-22 pure-logic component pc-check-weighted-entries with name/description/content only. The body reads every raw field via inputs.get (never direct access), validates the list shape and each item's exact label/weight types and bounds before computing eligibility, and returns {ok, entries} with the original list only when valid and [] otherwise. It makes zero host calls, imports, I/O or coercions; booleans are rejected as integers; missing and null are distinguished; extra item fields fail closed. The list cardinality contract is 0..3 inclusive (empty valid), so a four-item list is rejected before any effect. This is an unapproved draft and a target typed-input interface; typed runner support and Q1/Q2 approval precede activation. No other proposal arrays were populated per the test scope.",
  "proposed_recipe_updates": [],
  "adjusted_volatile_messages": [
    ["user", "Validate raw weighted entries, including an empty selection."]
  ],
  "proposed_components": [
    {
      "class_code": 22,
      "payload": {
        "name": "pc-check-weighted-entries",
        "description": "Pure-logic guard that validates a raw list of weighted entries and returns whether it is well-formed. The list must have 0..3 items inclusive (empty is valid). Each item must be a JSON object with exactly the fields label and weight: label is a string of length 1..8 inclusive, weight is an exact integer 0..1 inclusive, never a boolean or float. Missing, null, extra item fields or invalid shapes fail closed without exceptions. Returns {ok: boolean, entries: original list if valid else []}. No imports, host calls, I/O or type coercion.",
        "content": "def classify_entry(item):
    if not isinstance(item, dict):
        return False
    if 'label' not in item or 'weight' not in item:
        return False
    if len(item) != 2:
        return False
    label = item.get('label')
    weight = item.get('weight')
    if not (type(label) is str and 1 <= len(label) <= 8):
        return False
    if not (type(weight) is int and not isinstance(weight, bool) and 0 <= weight <= 1):
        return False
    return True

def check_weighted_entries(entries):
    if not isinstance(entries, list) or len(entries) > 3:
        return {'ok': False, 'entries': []}
    valid = True
    for item in entries:
        if not classify_entry(item):
            valid = False
            break
    result = {'ok': valid, 'entries': entries if valid else []}
    return result
result = check_weighted_entries(inputs.get('entries'))"
      }
    }
  ],
  "settings_adjustments": []
  ,
  "bridge_messages": []
}
